# Placeholder to ensure the `assets/` tree (declared in cartridge.json) is
# represented in packed .car archives.
#
# rglob + zip in the packer only includes *files*; without at least one file
# under assets/, extractall would not create the assets/ directory, causing
# load_archive to raise "Cartridge assets directory missing".
#
# tgl_demo keeps its real sprites in the engine's asset roots (precedence
# after P1-A) and uses this dir only for the mount contract / future private
# assets. The scaffold creates either a player.png or .gitkeep for the same
# reason.
#
# This makes `py2d-cartridge tgl_demo` produce a .car that fully roundtrips
# (load_archive succeeds and behaves like directory mode for the reference).
